      "text": [
        " لِأَبِي اَلْحَسَنِ مُوسَى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِمَا اَلسَّلاَمُ أُحِبُّ أَنْ تَدَعَنِي عَلَى أَنْ أُكَفِّنَكَ فَقَالَ «إِنَّا أَهْلُ بَيْتٍ حَجُّ صَرُورَتِنَا وَ مُهُورُ نِسَائِنَا وَ أَكْفَانُنَا مِنْ طَهُورِ أَمْوَالِنَا."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.577 - It is narrated that Al-Sindi ibn Shahak said to Abu Al-Hasan Imam Musa ibn Jafar Al-Kadhim (as) ; \"I would like you to allow me to provide your shroud.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"We, the people of the household (AhlulBayt (as)), have our pilgrimage, dowries of our women, and shrouds taken from the purity of our own wealth.\""
        ]
      }
